{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592243-what-are-your-thoughts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game","id":592243,"title":"What are your thoughts on a WoD: Buffyverse game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-15T20:14:16-07:00","id":592243,"title":"What are your thoughts on a WoD: Buffyverse game?","content":"So, I've been playing the Unisystem for 10 or more years (mainly Cinematic) now and after all this time my Boys finally have wanted to join a game. So, I introduced them to Unisystem, which they liked but were interested in the White-Wolf setting. So, after a few game sessions we've decided to run a Buffyverse game using the CWoD (classic white-wolf). I have done extensive research over the net to see if anyone else has done this and I have found several fanfics that use both settings, but I was wondering what are your thoughts on adapting (converting, etc) the Slayer and her scoobies?<br /> <br /> I await your replies...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","name":"Superior1200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T21:02:02-07:00","id":592280,"title":"","content":"I think the White Wolf rules system is ideal for portraying very versatile characters and helps in portraying a story over action scenes and other types of experiences. Buffy usually has a pretty good story.<br /> <br /> But a lot of content for WoD focuses on the corrupt nature of the world and the people who live in it. Lots of material you can pretty much chuck out the window for a Buffyverse style game, which is far lighter and resides in a world <i>where the heroes can win.</i> In WoD, the apocalypse is inevitable. The world is rotting away, and everything is going down the drain.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of pros to running your Buffy game in the WoD rules set (especially if players are already familiar with it). It's much better at social and dramatic encounters.<br /> If you're looking to run a more pulpy action-oriented game with a variety of combat scenarios, I'd recommend using the Savage Worlds rules system.<br /> <br /> Using World of Darkness, you could probably use the rules for Shih character creation out of <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/337/World-of-Darkness-Demon-Hunter-X?term=demon+hunter+x&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Hunter X</a> to represent a Slayer pretty effectively (in terms of stats and martial prowess).<br /> As for the Scoobies? World of Darkness has a PLETHORA of gorgeous books to help flesh out mortals. If you're looking for ways to represent Willow's magey pursuits, check the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/263/Sorcerer-Revised-Edition?term=sorcerer+revised+&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer Revised Edition</a>. For everyone else, you could run using the Bystander rules out of <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/639/Hunter-The-Reckoning?term=Hunter%3A+The+Reck&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> without too much trouble. Just, make Conviction easier to work with to reflect the less grim and hopeless game world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","user":"DarkExcalibur42","date":". 07-16-2015, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T21:04:12-07:00","id":592282,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/291/The-Inquisition?term=inquisiti&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">The Inquisition</a> or <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/147/Halls-of-the-Arcanum?term=halls&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Halls of the Arcanum</a> might be useful to portray a Watcher. Both of which are represented in the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114261/The-Hunters-Hunted-II?term=hunters+hunted\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter's Hunted 2</a> (a truly fantastic book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T21:23:38-07:00","id":592290,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the reply and the information. I totally forgot about Demon Hunter X and I do own the 20th Anniversary items on pdf and book, so I guess a little more research is needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","user":"Superior1200","date":". 07-16-2015, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","name":"Superior1200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T09:31:52-07:00","id":592770,"title":"","content":"This depends what you're doing. While the settings have some overlap, I'm a fan of both but not of mixing them. (This year I ran <b>Buffy</b> in the afternoon and <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> in the evening at my local games society, and deliberately focused on the differences between the two, making the former light and monster-of-the-week and the latter political and dramatic. I joked about using the same plot for both games but didn't actually do it...)<br /> <br /> Having a heroic Vampire Slayer is problematic in a setting where vampires can be considered to have souls (even if they don't all keep them in good working order) so that might not be a good combination. On the other hand having different &quot;clans&quot; of vampires with different powers and interests would not be a stretch for the Buffyverse. Pick and choose concepts rather than trying to combine the cosmologies.<br /> <br /> Hunting monsters in the World Of Darkness is more about stealth and ambushes than straight-up combat. If I were using the Storyteller System I'd probably borrow Dramatic Editing from <b><i>Adventure!</i></b> to make the game less dangerous to mortal PCs who get into fights with monsters on a weekly basis. I'd rather use the tailor-made <b>Buffy</b> game and import some ideas, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T11:28:56-07:00","id":592960,"title":"","content":"Personaly, if you want to use the setting of cWoD and similar rules, I would recomend to look for the nWoD. There you will have more solid rules specially for Mortal PCs. It isn't much of a stretch to use it even to portray the cWoD setting. You'll already needing to stretch things just to make it more Buffyverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T12:37:19-07:00","id":593021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592243-what-are-your-thoughts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game?p=592960#post592960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personaly, if you want to use the setting of cWoD and similar rules, I would recomend to look for the nWoD. There you will have more solid rules specially for Mortal PCs. It isn't much of a stretch to use it even to portray the cWoD setting. You'll already needing to stretch things just to make it more Buffyverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are already mountains of cWoD books that handle mortals in the WoD... are the new books that much better?<br /> <br /> Anyway, as far as a Buffyverse game goes, there are always those other characters with something special about them! Vampires with souls, witches, watchers, werewolves, friendly demons... I think a lot of what you do will be looking for ways to tweak standard WoD to allow these flavor variations!<br /> <br /> Want to do some special agency that polices the supernatural?<br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/235/Project-Twilight\" target=\"_blank\">Project Twilight</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/337/World-of-Darkness-Demon-Hunter-X\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Hunter X</a><br /> Need some holy warriors to roll in and mess up the way your team does things?<br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/291/The-Inquisition\" target=\"_blank\">The Inquisition</a><br /> Need a touch of magic?<br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/147/Halls-of-the-Arcanum\" target=\"_blank\">Halls of the Arcanum</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/263/Sorcerer-Revised-Edition\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer Revised</a><br /> Want to run with heroes who have sold their souls to demons?<br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/99/Damned-and-Deceived\" target=\"_blank\">Damned and Deceived</a><br /> Need to give your standard players something to fight with?<br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/459/The-Hunters-Hunted-WW2205\" target=\"_blank\">The Hunter's Hunted</a> / <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114261/The-Hunters-Hunted-II\" target=\"_blank\">The Hunter's Hunted II</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/638/Hunter-Players-Guide?manufacturers_id=1&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter Player's Guide</a> (has rules for playing as bystanders!)<br /> <br /> Need some unusual creatures to fill in the gaps of your campaign?<br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/50/Bygone-Bestiary?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Bygone Bestiary</a><br /> Need a super-villain?<br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/119/Earthbound?manufacturers_id=1&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Earthbound</a> / <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1545/Hunter-The-Infernal?term=Hunter%3A+Infernal&amp;manufacturers_id=1&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter: The Infernal</a><br /> <br /> Want to run with some Werewolves? Here's my standard Werewolf nerf using <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/50/Bygone-Bestiary?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Bygone Bestiary</a>:<br /> 1.) Basically ignore the Werewolf books. They're just too powerful to play nice with your mortals, or anything else.<br /> 2.) Give shifters 3 forms: human, animal (out of Bygone Bestiary, minus legendary powers), and hybrid.<br /> 3.) Determine Hybrid stats as follows:<br /> a. Add the animal's physical stats and add these values as attribute bonuses (I used stats out of Bygone Bestiary, so Werewolves got +2 Strength, +2 Dexterity, +3 Stamina).<br /> b. Also gain these abilities in Hybrid &amp; Animal forms:<br /> - Gain the <i>Acute Sense</i> Merit (1 point). Grant the player a -2 reduction in difficulty checks for Perception rolls made with the animal's favored sense (scent is easier for werewolves, sight is easier for crows, etc)<br /> - Gain Nightsight (3pt power, Bygone Bestiary).<br /> - Gain <i>Vulnerability to Silver</i> Flaw (3pts, again out of Bygone Bestiary).<br /> - Gain a Bite &amp; Claw attack (5pt power, Bygone Bestiary)<br /> - Gain Rapid Healing (6pt power, Bygone Bestiary).<br /> <br /> Total, playing a Werewolf this way I value at ~50 Freebie points. Which obviously none of your players could have at character creation unless you're going to go with some sort of veterancy rules and allow some to start at higher Experience levels (and trade Experience for Freebies). I think taking every Bystander Merit would put you at like 17 Freebie points spent (not counting however you want to value them having a Conviction score, which might be something you just blanket give to ALL your players).<br /> <br /> Side Note: if you do give all your players Conviction, I'd recommend letting players who buy Psychic or Magic numina spend their Conviction instead of Willpower to use those powers. Same goes for if you use a Werewolf player. Maybe let him spend Experience to buy things like the ability to instantly heal wounds for Conviction. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Seeing as you're going for a pulpier genre with a happier atmosphere, you could lift some of the restrictions on True Faith and make it easier for a player to run with that numina too.<br /> <br /> On top of all this stuff? There are a lot of Merits and Flaws with clear Supernatural themes that you could let players use to flesh themselves out in unique ways.<br /> \u2022 Innocent (The Inquistion)<br /> \u2022 Supernatural Affinity (Hunter: Player's Guide)<br /> \u2022 Supernatural Companion (Halls of the Arcanum)<br /> \u2022 Burning/Holy Aura (Halls of the Arcanum / Inquisition)<br /> \u2022 Ecstatic (Inquisition)<br /> \u2022 Pale Aura (Hunter's Hunted)<br /> \u2022 Psychic Awareness (Halls of the Arcanum)<br /> \u2022 Soothing Voice (Inquisition)<br /> \u2022 Symbol of Independence (Inquisition)<br /> \u2022 Ecumenist (Inquisition)<br /> \u2022 Invisible (Hunter's Hunted)<br /> \u2022 Precognition (Halls of the Arcanum)<br /> \u2022 Prophetic Ability (Inquisition)<br /> \u2022 Sorcerous Awareness (Inquisition) - You may want to combine this and Psychic Awareness into one merit<br /> \u2022 Clear Sighted (Hunter's Hunted / Halls of the Arcanum)<br /> \u2022 Fountain of Life (Inquisition)<br /> \u2022 Ghoul (Hunter's Hunted) - YES! You could have a player who was a ghoul... maybe killing vampires to drink their blood and sate that addiction.<br /> \u2022 Fist of God (Hunter's Hunted) - This one costs 7 points and is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","user":"DarkExcalibur42","date":". 07-16-2015, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T15:24:19-07:00","id":593207,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking of doing something similar, good stuff in here on how to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5176-curlyinsaneguy","name":"CurlyInsaneGuy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T17:54:17-07:00","id":593405,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Wow, I didn't think outside the box for most of these source books...<br /> I do have some ideas for creating characters using the idea out of Buffy the Vampire Slayer (White-Hats and Heroes) character types, as below</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Getting Started<br /> The character-creation system is designed around five basic precepts. Keep these in mind while generating the persona you will assume in the Buffyverse.<br /> \u2022 Just like it says in Vampire the Masquerade (20th Anniversary; see page 79) core book: You may create a character of any age, from any culture and from any nation, subject to the Storyteller\u2019s (Director\u2019s for my world) approval.<br /> \u2022 The character creation system is intended more as a persona development device than as a strict mechanical system. Although, all Cast Members start out as Mortals.<br /> \u2022 Players still have a certain number of points to spend on Traits they would like their character to have. Players also get \u201cfreebie points\u201d at the end of character creation to round out their Cast Member.<br /> \u2022 A Trait of 1 is poor, while a rating of 5 is excellent. Thus, a character with a single dot in a Trait is either not very good with that Trait or is a beginner.<br /> \u2022 It is the player\u2019s responsibility to take on the role of their Cast Member that\u2019s not detrimental to the story over all.<br /> <br /> Advanced Characters (Optional)<br /> Seasoned Cast Members: 35 experience points.<br /> Expert Cast Members: 75 experience points.<br /> Veteran Cast Members: 100 experience points.<br /> <br /> Character Creation Table<br /> This covers the character creation process in short form; refer to the appropriate sections for details. Available Points are listed where relevant.<br /> <br /> STAGE ONE: BEING HUMAN<br /> Here you decide what your Cast Member was like prior to his transformation. For all intents and purposes, you are creating a normal human being.<br /> <br /> Step One: Concept<br /> Choose Concept, Nature and Demeanor. (Refer to Vampire the Masquerade or the many Core Books available for more details).<br /> <br /> Step Two: Select Attributes<br /> Prioritize the three areas: Physical, Social, and Mental (7/5/3 Heroes; 6/4/3 White-Hats).<br /> Choose primary Attributes (7 or 6 points)<br /> Choose secondary Attributes (5 or 4 points)<br /> Choose tertiary Attributes (3 points)<br /> <br /> Step Three: Select Abilities<br /> Prioritize the three areas: Talents, Skills, and Knowledges (13/9/5 Heroes; 11/7/4 White-Hats).<br /> No Ability higher than 3 at this stage.<br /> .<br /> Step Four: Backgrounds<br /> Choose Backgrounds (5)<br /> <br /> Step Five: Finishing Touches<br /> Record Humanity (7), Willpower (5 Heroes; 3 White-Hats).<br /> Spend Freebie Points (15 Heroes; 21 White-Hats).<br /> Optional: Choose Merits and Flaws (max. 7 points).<br /> <br /> STAGE TWO: SUPERNATURAL TRANSFORMATION<br /> Now you know what your Cast Member is like. Or rather, what she was like before her transformation.<br /> <br /> Step One: Supernatural Transformation<br /> Determine (or Director assigns during play) the type of transformation your Cast Member undergoes:<br /> Choose Slayer, Vampire, Werewolf, Sorceror, and Demon/Half-Demon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, before you get started, I originally thought about building Templates (similar to nWoD) with basic attribute/ability enhancements, powers (disciplines, magick, etc.) and what have you for balancing purposes. Just haven't decided.<br /> When I mentioned using the cWoD system, it was just for the system itself not setting related material. Hope this kind of helps out on how I'm seeing things.<br /> <br /> Ron","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","user":"Superior1200","date":". 07-16-2015, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","name":"Superior1200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T17:59:36-07:00","id":593408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592243-what-are-your-thoughts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game?p=593021#post593021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are already mountains of cWoD books that handle mortals in the WoD... are the new books that much better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. They are.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I'm an old fan of WoD as well, since the 90's, but the new rules ARE more solid, SPECIALY for mortal characters. And also for a lot of the other things out there.<br /> <br /> For a game focused around mortals, even if not normal ones, and where you need a lot of stuff to be uncommon, believe me, nWoD can do a better job with less material and with less thinkering of said material.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying nWoD is a perfect substitute for cWoD. I do post on this forum after all, I'm still a cWoD fan. But given the focus of the game, I can guarantee nWoD will do a better job by far.<br /> <br /> Just with the 2nd edition core WoD book, or the 1st edition and the God Machine Chronicle rules update, you already covers a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T18:17:31-07:00","id":593417,"title":"","content":"I'll admit my solution involves reaching into varying and disparate rules books! Though.... I kinda like doing that, too. So the inconvenience is almost a selling point for me &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> Good to know about the new books though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T21:19:14-07:00","id":593505,"title":"","content":"I did find someone's fanfic where they explained the Buffyeverse merging with the cWoD setting. I do believe he did a heck of a job and it could make since. Explains how the two verses can coexist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","name":"Superior1200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T23:25:26-07:00","id":593605,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would take only the aspects or flavor of a Buffy game that I wanted and largely ignore the Buffyverse continuity in favor of whatever I wanted to tell for a story. Rather than a Buffy game, I'd run a Buffy INSPIRED game. Maybe have something like the high school library meeting zone where our would-be heroes meet to see how bad it really is (which is the iconic Buffy scene).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T00:27:45-07:00","id":593616,"title":"","content":"I thought he was after something more buffy-like instead of just a buffy-inspired cWoD chronicle. That's why I recomended nWoD. You will find better rules to do:<br /> <br /> 1- Human characters that stand by themselfs system-wise. The system is made primarily for humans.<br /> <br /> 2- Crossovers. The system was built both to balance splats and, more to the point, to make those splats work on rules that actualy mean something for the others. No time lost figuring out the Humanity rating of the Werewolf, or the Banality of the Ghost. That also aplies to skills.<br /> <br /> 3- Weird phenomena. Just peruse the &quot;Blue Line&quot; and you'll see simpler rules to make strange stuff happen.<br /> <br /> Most of your work will be done already. And you can simply (given the proposal) ignore setting content if you like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T01:12:12-07:00","id":593628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592243-what-are-your-thoughts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game?p=593616#post593616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought he was after something more buffy-like instead of just a buffy-inspired cWoD chronicle. .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I mean: a Buffy-inspired plot (with all new characters and setting) in a Buffy-like universe using existing World of Darkness books.<br /> <br /> Rather than making a new spin-off series. New world means new secrets for your players to uncover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T22:53:23-07:00","id":594461,"title":"","content":"The idea is to run a Buffyverse game.<br /> A new Slayer and a new gang of scoobies within a new town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","name":"Superior1200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T04:56:20-07:00","id":594640,"title":"","content":"In that case, you'll want to twist or modify a lot of the books and implementation.<br /> <br /> I still think treating all your players like Hunter Bystanders with modified Conviction rules is the best way to go. If one player learns Hedge Magic? Let them spend Conviction instead of Willpower to use it. Decide how many of the Bystander Traits you want and just blanket give them to all your players free of charge.<br /> <br /> The Shih remain a good choice for how to portray a Slayer, making Demon Hunter X a very useful book. But there are other ways to do it, too. If you have a copy of Vampire, using stuff out of that book (like Potence or Celerity) might be a good way to portray the power level of a Slayer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:26:29-07:00","id":594829,"title":"","content":"Here's the idea on the Slayer:<br /> <br /> When the Slayer is first &quot;Called,&quot; her physical attributes all immediately become fives, and she gains a point each of Potence, Celerity, and Fortitude. She can add to these disciplines with training and experience. Her Brawl, Dodge, Melee, Athletics, Archery, and Firearms immediately become threes. In addition, her healing abilities are vastly increased. The Health levels that take months to heal, heal in as many weeks. Those that take weeks, take as many days, and those that take days, hours. She also gains other, less tangible powers: sharper senses (as the merits), prophetic dreams, and the ability to sense vampires.<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","name":"Superior1200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:48:34-07:00","id":594859,"title":"","content":"Actually if I was going to run a Buffyverse game I'd use Adventure. Most of the Slayer's abilities can be found in Daredevil knacks and adding in Dramatic editing would cut down on deaths. <br /> The villain of the week could easily be built using the same system.<br /> <br /> If using CWoD for the Slayer use Werewolf rules, regenerates 1 health level per rd for bashing, and 1 health level an hour for lethal. Give her Sense the Unnatural to detect all kinds of critters, but make vamps difficulty low. I also might give the Slayer Rage without frenzy. Soak will be a problem, I like the fortitude idea but am not sold on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:42:26-07:00","id":594881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Superior1200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592243-what-are-your-thoughts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game?p=594829#post594829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the idea on the Slayer:<br /> <br /> When the Slayer is first &quot;Called,&quot; her physical attributes all immediately become fives, and she gains a point each of Potence, Celerity, and Fortitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some slayers are faster, some are stronger, some can take a hit better. Don't take away their originality and uniqueness. Plus, Slayers are generally super-human in all of these attributes. I'd say give them between a +2 and +4 bonus to all 3 attributes (depending on how you run other aspects of it, like mixing in Potence/Celerity/Fortitude). Their origin matters, and just setting them all to 5's reduces an aspect of that character origin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She can add to these disciplines with training and experience. Her Brawl, Dodge, Melee, Athletics, Archery, and Firearms immediately become threes. </div> </div> </div>You don't want to auto-set people's attributes. If you're going to do that, you should just make your own Slayer character sheet and issue it to players.<br /> <br /> It's okay for newbie Slayers to suck at these things! Let them develop, spend their XP, get trained by Watchers. Alternately, if you're starting a game with an established team tell your Slayer that X amount of her XP has to be spent on raising these to a minimum level (which I would set at 2 dots. let them specialize).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition, her healing abilities are vastly increased. The Health levels that take months to heal, heal in as many weeks. Those that take weeks, take as many days, and those that take days, hours. She also gains other, less tangible powers: sharper senses (as the merits), prophetic dreams, and the ability to sense vampires. </div> </div> </div>I'd use Bygone Bestiary's Rapid Healing (it lets you treat wounds as lower wound categories for healing, varying based on how many points you invest in it).<br /> <br /> The Prophetic Dreams and Heightened Senses could (at least partly) be represented by dots of Awareness. If you want, give her a difficulty reduction in detecting vampires with Alertness/Perception rolls. Again, Bygone Bestiary has something you could use for Prophetic Dreams (so does Hunter's Vision creed, IIRC). But those dreams are plot devices too, so honestly don't need to be represented mechanically. They're part of your story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592243-what-are-your-thoughts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game?p=594859#post594859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If using CWoD for the Slayer use Werewolf rules, regenerates 1 health level per rd for bashing, and 1 health level an hour for lethal. Give her Sense the Unnatural to detect all kinds of critters, but make vamps difficulty low. I also might give the Slayer Rage without frenzy. Soak will be a problem, I like the fortitude idea but am not sold on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never use Werewolf rules. ESPECIALLY never use Werewolf rules for mortal themed games. Werewolf are disgustingly powerful to a nuisance level, and only balance out in their own world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T14:45:26-07:00","id":595023,"title":"","content":"Man, with all of these ideas, its beginning to seem more complicated then I first thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","name":"Superior1200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T16:09:12-07:00","id":595105,"title":"","content":"In nWoD you could just use Core, Hunter: The Vigil, Second Sight, and the core of each splat you want to see your PCs stealing some powers. 2nd edition works better. For the Slayer, you could borrow and reinterpret the rules for Slashers.<br /> <br /> Natura regeneration is already better for mortals, and you can make it even better without much of a problem.<br /> <br /> Sorry for insisting on nWoD here, but I really think it to be a lot better to the proposed chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T17:18:55-07:00","id":595155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Superior1200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592243-what-are-your-thoughts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game?p=595023#post595023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, with all of these ideas, its beginning to seem more complicated then I first thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Running custom games is never simple. You're basically writing your own splat as you go! That's why I recommend stealing as much as you can from existing materials.<br /> <br /> The biggest decision making issue here is how powerful you want Slayers to be, and what overall party balance you'd like to see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592243-what-are-your-thoughts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game?p=595105#post595105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In nWoD you could just use Core, Hunter: The Vigil, Second Sight, and the core of each splat you want to see your PCs stealing some powers. 2nd edition works better. For the Slayer, you could borrow and reinterpret the rules for Slashers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could already do that using Hunter: The Reckoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","user":"DarkExcalibur42","date":". 07-18-2015, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T18:23:16-07:00","id":595199,"title":"","content":"I meant, do everything he wants to do just with those books. Not just the Slayer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T18:27:26-07:00","id":595215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592243-what-are-your-thoughts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game?p=595199#post595199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant, do everything he wants to do just with those books. Not just the Slayer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using just the Hunter: The Reckoning and/or the Player's Guide he could represent all of his party members. The Slayer would require some home-brew.<br /> If you wanted to throw in magic, add Sorcerer Revised or I think the Hunter's Hunted 2 has good stuff in it.<br /> <br /> Still only 2 books. That's why I'm not seeing the big advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T22:08:07-07:00","id":599036,"title":"","content":"I've started seeing that the players were still focusing on the actual &quot;World of Darkness&quot; setting versus the Buffyverse setting....Probably need to figure out away to break free from the WoD setting...choices","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","name":"Superior1200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T01:03:24-07:00","id":599078,"title":"","content":"Show them. Let them think things work like they do in the WoD, then just land infectious vampires on them or put them up against a Blood God or Demon Invasion which they can only beat by using old books, tricks and DRAMAAAAA!!!!!11","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T02:10:57-07:00","id":599095,"title":"","content":"I'm curious as to why Sorcerer for witches in Buffy as opposed to Awakened Magic. Willow could do a lot more than your average Sorcerer and A LOT faster even when starting out. Granted Willow herself is a bit of a prodigy but Sorcery paths are no where near the level of power any of the witches portrayed on the show display. I'm not saying anybody is wrong but I am curious as to the preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T16:20:05-07:00","id":599948,"title":"","content":"I'd make the Slayer a Dhampir without Vampire parents and raise blood and discipline caps to 13th Gen levels ie 10 BP, 1 BP/turn, D-Max 5. As she kills vampires and what not, the ST can award the Slayer with a &quot;generation&quot; to improve her limits.<br /> Alternatively, you could make her a Kami from the Possessed Book to represent Sync with the Slayer Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T17:21:30-07:00","id":599998,"title":"","content":"There was a cWoD-inspired Buffy game a while back. I tracked it down here: <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20071107195516/http://www.tucsonpages.com/buffy/online/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://web.archive.org/web/200711071...ine/index.html</a>. I tried downloading it, but it's an executable file that tries to open some format that probably hasn't been used in a decade or more...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyo