houghts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game?p=599078#post599078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Show them. Let them think things work like they do in the WoD, then just land infectious vampires on them or put them up against a Blood God or Demon Invasion which they can only beat by using old books, tricks and DRAMAAAAA!!!!!11</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/592243-what-are-your-thoughts-on-a-wod-buffyverse-game?p=599095#post599095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious as to why Sorcerer for witches in Buffy as opposed to Awakened Magic. Willow could do a lot more than your average Sorcerer and A LOT faster even when starting out. Granted Willow herself is a bit of a prodigy but Sorcery paths are no where near the level of power any of the witches portrayed on the show display. I'm not saying anybody is wrong but I am curious as to the preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only when she went CRAZY O.P. AND EVIL... aka passed from player control to GM control, becoming a story villain instead of character.<br /> <br /> Game balance. Sorcerer is more balanced than Awakened Magey stuff, which is utterly bullshit with how powerful it is. Same reason I recommended a heavy nerf to Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T14:00:34-07:00","id":603181,"title":"","content":"I managed to convert that Buffy game to PDF here: <a href=\"https://www.wetransfer.com/downloads/b7bab0d013b630990232e75a36adc58020150725205512/32730d4ab0f56d329a08c5c538fff4e720150725205512/f6804a\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.wetransfer.com/downloads...5205512/f6804a</a>.<br /> <br /> Note that the pics aren't very good on it, because it was a really outdated format. The rules are like a stripped back version of Storyteller, so it'd be easy enough to just use oWoD rules with the new rules for powers and character types to make things easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T18:30:14-07:00","id":605167,"title":"","content":"Its got a lot of black lines in various places, so I'll see what I can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6939-superior1200","name":"Superior1200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","val